Original commit body from c04ddad59347a8d7c58cbfc0692ebbc89ff09bd2:

The __init__ field scan matched only ast.Assign, so an annotated
`self.x: T = v` (or bare `self.x: T`) was skipped entirely — the field was
captured neither into the class's meta["fields"] type map nor into
own_field_names. An annotated own field therefore stayed eligible for a
confidently-wrong Site-3 hint to a same-named PARENT field of a different type.

The scan now normalizes ast.Assign and ast.AnnAssign to a common
(targets, value) shape before the self-attribute check, so annotated own fields
are captured identically.

Scope: WI-sajub Issue 1 (AnnAssign). Issue 2 — the same-name-class short-name
clobber in the meta["fields"] attach (two classes, one short name -> recall
loss) — remains the deferred id-keyed follow-up already documented in-code
(py.py class_own_field_names comment); it needs a class_symbol_by_node_id map
and re-keying the name-keyed consumer dicts.

WI-sajub (G5). Advances; Issue 2 residual remains.

